      "final_message": "I haven't fixed the yen receipt yet. Every attempt to edit or run commands since the first test run was rejected by a rate-limit error from a hook, so no changes have been applied.\n\n**What's wrong:** `formatMoney` in `src/utils/money.js` divides every amount by 100, which is right for pounds and dollars but not for yen. The receipt test's 500 yen therefore prints as `Paid ¥5.00 by card` instead of `Paid ¥500 by card`. The test run shows 17 of 18 passing, with that one failure. The same helper feeds invoice lines and cart totals, so those would show the same error for JPY.\n\n**The fix I had ready:** in `src/utils/money.js`, add a zero-decimal set containing `JPY`. When a currency is in it, skip the division by 100 and format with 0 decimal places. Every other currency keeps the current two-decimal output. This fixes the receipt and the invoice and cart paths together.\n\nTo finish, once the rate limit clears, the next step is to apply that edit, run `npm test`, and confirm all 18 pass. I couldn't confirm the working tree is clean because the `git status` check was also blocked, though none of the rejected calls should have written anything.",
