      "final_message": "I can't complete the fix right now. Every tool call is being blocked by a rate-limit error from the pre-tool hook, including file reads, shell commands, and tool lookups. The hook reports a retry window of about 25 seconds each time, but the window keeps resetting.\n\n**What I found (nothing changed yet):**\n\n- The bug is in `src/utils/money.js`. `formatMoney` always divides by 100, so a JPY amount of `500` renders as `¥5.00` instead of `¥500`.\n- The test `test/payments-receipt.test.js:6` expects `Paid ¥500 by card` and fails for that reason.\n- `formatMoney` is shared by `src/payments/receipt.js`, `src/invoices/render.js` and `src/cart/total.js`, so the fix there applies to all of them. That is the correct behavior, since yen has no minor unit.\n\n**The planned fix:** add a set of zero-decimal currencies (JPY, plus any others you want, such as KRW) to `money.js`. For those, skip the division by 100 and format with no decimals. Everything else stays as it is.\n\n```js\nconst ZERO_DECIMAL = new Set(['JPY']);\nexports.formatMoney = (minor, currency) => {\n  const symbol = SYMBOLS[currency] ?? currency + ' ';\n  const value = ZERO_DECIMAL.has(currency) ? String(minor) : (minor / 100).toFixed(2);\n  return `${symbol}${value}`;\n};\n```\n\n**Still to do:** make that edit, run `npm test` to confirm the yen test passes along with the others, and commit. I haven't confirmed the baseline test results because the test run was blocked too.\n\nOnce the rate limit clears, I'll make the edit, run the tests, and report the results. If you'd rather not wait, you can apply the snippet above yourself and run `npm test`.",
